sn11.17:1.4 starts: Then Sakka, lord of the devas, recited this verse
sn11.21:1.3 starts: Standing to one side, Sakka, lord of the devas, addressed
sn11.9:1.4 starts: “Vepacitti, lord of the asuras, put on his boots
sn12.17:2.5 none
sn12.17:2.9 starts: “Then ask what you want,
sn12.25:2.2 starts: some ascetics and brahmins, proponents of kamma, maintain that pleasure and pain are created by another;
sn12.25:7.1 starts: The Blessed One said: “Good, good, Ānanda!
